            "Cook and Campbell (1979) made it clear that all questions of external validity, or generalizability, are implicitly questions about interactions between the independent variable (treatment) and contextual variables such as participant selection, history, and research setting, so the quest for external validity is essentially a search for moderators that limit or qualify the cause-effect relationship.",
